    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7eEDz6",
      "title": "Type A Migration Exercise Tasks",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1430,
      "body": "Scaffold migrations-sop-1 chain migration tasks (076–081)\r\n\r\nAdds six sepolia tasks for migrating the migrations-sop-1 devnet (chainId 420120110) from Partner-operated to OP-operated infrastructure:\r\n\r\n076 — add FaultDisputeGame (game type 0) via OPCM\r\n077 — set OptimismPortal respected game type to 0\r\n078 — transfer SystemConfig ownership from Partner EOA → OPE Admin Safe (EOA-signed off-chain; ships as documented cast send flow)\r\n079 — set OP batcher + unsafe block signer\r\n080 — rotate PDG proposer to OP via DisputeGameFactory.setImplementation\r\n081 — upgrade fee-vault proxies to OP recipients via L1→L2 deposit\r\nEach task ships config.toml, addresses.json (fallback — chain not in superchain-registry), README.md, VALIDATION.md, and .env. <TBD_*> placeholders mark chain-specific values (prestate, ProxyAdmin, PDG game args, fee-vault impls, Safe nonces) the operator fills in at execution time.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-21T18:44:32Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1214,
      "deletions": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM6y-zCT",
      "title": "feat: add rehearsal task for governance upgrade",
      "author": "0xniha",
      "number": 1289,
      "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nThis PR adds **Rehearsal 4: Governor Upgrade**, enabling the Security Council to practice upgrading the Optimism Governor contract through an L1 deposit.\r\n\r\n### Task Implementation\r\n\r\n- [Task](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1289/files#diff-9ab92e2a7d110692ff8ef2e8777e37d94ec13890db31484066a29f72d32293fb): Complete rehearsal task using the `L1PortalExecuteL2Call` template.\r\n- Implements governor upgrade execution via L1 deposit transaction.\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\n- [Security Council Workflow](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1289/files#diff-d18244057e7295c78d6353138c857f7952a1435813835cd421086dc722cf12ef): Step-by-step guide for Security Council members to execute the rehearsal.\r\n- [L2 Simulation Guide](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1289/files#diff-eb55b8e65db3f4deeb5169d7163019d8b170392fa560dff9a8ec3b82a2596e99): Detailed walkthrough for manually simulating the L2 upgrade execution in Tenderly.\r\n  > **State Override Required**: The simulation requires setting `OptimismGovernorProxy` admin to `L2ProxyAdmin` via state override, because assumes this ownership to perform the upgrade.\r\n\r\n## Additional Changes\r\n\r\n- Fixed incorrect file paths in documentation references in [`README.md`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1289/files#diff-b335630551682c19a781afebcf4d07bf978fb1f8ac04c6bf87428ed5106870f5).",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2025-11-12T13:19:55Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 371,
      "deletions": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7LgNVK",
      "title": "Fee vault upgrade template - FeeVaultUpgrader",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1387,
      "body": "Fee vault upgrade template based on FeeVaultUpgrader.\r\n\r\nIt differs from the template #1381 because this one deploys new FeeVault implementation contracts to L2 and upgrades the proxies to them via upgradeAndCall + setRecipient in one atomic batch (v1.6.0 settable-recipient approach). UpdateFeeVaultRecipient in #1381 assumes implementations are already deployed and simply calls upgradeTo to point the proxies at them (immutable-recipient approach). ",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-03-18T11:01:35Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 318,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM68gXJD",
      "title": "opcm.update prestate template",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1336,
      "body": "Update prestate template for OPCMv600/U18",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
